DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Temporary Changes to Referral and Authorizati
 on Processes Ending November 30\, 2026
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Temporary Changes to Referral and Authorization Process
 es Ending November 30\, 2026\nTemporary Changes to Referral and Authorizat
 ion Processes Ending November 30\, 2026\nSep 08\, 2026\nBeginning\nDecembe
 r 1\, 2026\n\, the Department will require members to complete a Single A
 ssessment within the past 12 months before processing referrals\, prior
  authorization requests\, and continued stay reviews for children’s me
 dium- and high-intensity services.\nAs\npreviously communicated\n\, the De
 partment temporarily reinstated direct-to-provider referral and prior auth
 orization processes while operational challenges with the Single Assessm
 ent process were being addressed. That temporary process will end November
  30\, 2026.\nThe Single Assessment process has stabilized significantly\, 
 with assessments now completed in an average of 7.5 business days after a 
 request is submitted.\nThank you for your continued partnership with the 
 Single Assessment process.\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provi
 der-bulletins/temporary-changes-referral-and-authorization-processes-endin
 g-november-30-2026-2026-09-08
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/temporary-
 changes-referral-and-authorization-processes-ending-november-30-2026-2026-
 09-08
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
