SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] General Election is two months away\; Secreta
 ry of State’s Office provides update on Maine election processes
DESCRIPTION:AUGUSTA\, MAINE\n– Today September 4\, marks just 60 days un
 til the General Election on November 3. The Office of the Secretary of Sta
 te today provided an update about Maine’s election processes for this st
 age of the election cycle.\nKey dates to know:\nSeptember 15 -\nNational V
 oter Registration Day\nSeptember 19 (45 days before Election Day) -\nDeadl
 ine to send UOCAVA ballots to already pending requests\nOctober 4 (30 days
  before Election Day) -\nIn-person\, no-excuse absentee voting period begi
 ns (goes through close of business in a voter's town on Thurs.\, October 2
 9)\nOctober 20 -\nElection Hero Day\nOctober 27 -\nMock Election Day\nOcto
 ber 29 - L\nast day to request a no-excuse absentee ballot\nRegistration d
 eadlines:\nIn person:\nClose of the polls on Election Day.\nRegistering by
  mail or 3rd person:\nReceived by the voter’s town or city by close of b
 usiness 21 days before Election Day. (October 13)\nRegistering online:\n5 
 PM on the 21st day before Election Day. (October 13)\nRegistration through
  the BMV:\nOn the 7th day before Election Day. (October 27)\nUOCAVA voters
  in Title 21-A section 777-A by mail or electronically:\nBy Noon the day b
 efore Election Day (November 2)\nAbsentee ballots:\nRequesting an absentee
  ballot\n: Absentee ballots\, including accessible ballots and ballots for
  uniformed and overseas voters\, may be requested online at\nmaine.gov/cgi
 -bin/online/AbsenteeBallot/index.pl\n. Voters may also contact their town 
 hall to request a ballot or submit a paper application for an absentee bal
 lot\, and the request must be received at least three business days before
  Election Day (October 29)\, unless special circumstances exist.\nReturnin
 g an absentee ballot:\nOnly ballots received by 8 p.m. on Election Day are
  counted\, regardless of postmark. In many towns and cities\, voters have 
 the option of returning an absentee ballot to a secured drop box. Maine vo
 ters can track the process of their ballot at:\napps.web.maine.gov/cgi-bin
 /online/AbsenteeBallot/ballot_status.pl\n.\nAbsentee ballot proce\nhttps:/
 /www.maine.gov/sos/news/general-election-two-months-away-secretary-states-
 office-provides-update-maine-election-1
URL:https://www.maine.gov/sos/news/general-election-two-months-away-secret
 ary-states-office-provides-update-maine-election-1
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
